---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base active="about" title="About" description="Who I am and what I'm working toward.">
  <article class="post">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{site.author}</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I work at the intersection of <strong>OSINT, red teaming, and AI agents</strong> — building
        systems that pull signal out of noise. Most of what I make starts with a simple question:
        <em>what can you learn without ever touching the target?</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now my focus is <strong>ShadowBroker</strong>, a global threat-intercept platform that
        aggregates open intelligence — aircraft, satellites, seismic activity, and more — into one
        interface, then lets AI agents find the correlations nobody was looking for. Alongside it
        I’m building passive recon engines, red-team automation, and tooling for bug hunters.
      </p>
      <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        Two reasons. First, a place to <strong>showcase the work</strong> — the projects below are
        the real output, not a résumé. Second, a <strong>journal</strong>: I’m documenting the build
        in public so the dead ends and breakthroughs are written down while they’re still fresh.
      </p>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Find me on <a href={site.links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> or reach out
        by <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>email</a>. I’m always up for a conversation about
        intelligence, offensive security, or where autonomous agents go next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .post {
    padding: 24px 0 20px;
  }
  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
</style>
